Submit one request per H.264 slice on a slice-based V4L2 decoder.

Apple's AVD, and the other mainline stateless decoders, take one slice
per media request. Every slice but the last is queued with
V4L2_BUF_FLAG_M2M_HOLD_CAPTURE_BUF, and the capture buffer is queued
only with the first slice. Chromium used to put the whole picture in
one request, so a second slice was rejected and meeting video fell
back to software.

The hold flag is used only when the OUTPUT queue advertises
V4L2_BUF_CAP_SUPPORTS_M2M_HOLD_CAPTURE_BUF and the decode mode is
slice-based. That capability is read after the coded format is set,
because AVD and cedrus publish it from S_FMT. A frame-based device,
and a picture with one slice, keep the single-request path.

